<title>FRANCE: EP approves faster tractors.</title>
<headline>EP approves faster tractors.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers in all European Union member states will in future be able to use tractors which can travel at 40km/h, following the European Parliament's decision on Tuesday to approve the plan.</p>
<p>Earlier this year the European Commission proposed a revision of European type-approval directives approved between 1974 and 1989, so as to increase the maximum permitted speed for tractors from 30 to 40km/h.</p>
<p>The proposal has the support of tractor manufacturers.</p>
<p>It requires the approval of both Parliament and ministers to become law.</p>
<p>Giving the measure a first reading on Tuesday, Euro-MPs said that if the EU was going to allow faster tractors, it should also impose stricter, more regular technical controls on these vehicles, clamp down on the pollution they cause and bring in EU-wide rules on safety, including the wearing of safety belts.</p>
</text>
